+{
+  "_about": "The first run's steps, in order (tools/first-run/first-run.mjs). DATA, not code: UI (who owns the menus) confirms or corrects the keys on the first click; a step that goes wrong is a line of the report, never a stop. A step: `human` (a sentence shown to the person at the PC; the run waits until the game's picture changes, which is how it sees that a person pressed Enter on the flashing-effects warning: the script NEVER presses through that warning), `keys` (ENTER ESC SPACE UP DOWN LEFT RIGHT P F1 TAB, pressed one after another), `settleMs` (wait before the still), `shot` (the still's file name), `crop` (x,y,w,h as fractions of the window, for a still of a part), `alsoCrop` (a second still of a part, from the same moment), `holdS` (wait after the step, seconds). The draft below follows the mode smoke's own walk (tools/smoke/mode_smoke.gd): the list of modes, Solo, a fighter, Start, play, Start for the pause card, Quit, the question with Stay lit, one Up to 'Close the game', Enter. DRAFT: unproven in a window.",
+  "steps": [
+    { "id": "notice", "what": "a person reads the flashing-effects warning and presses Enter in the game", "human": "The game is showing its warning about flashing effects. Read it, then press Enter IN THE GAME WINDOW. The test carries on by itself when it sees the picture change.", "humanLimitS": 300, "settleMs": 4000, "shot": "00-after-warning" },
+    { "id": "mode-list", "what": "the list of modes, with the version line", "settleMs": 2500, "shot": "01-mode-list", "alsoCrop": { "shot": "02-version-line", "crop": [0, 0.88, 1, 0.12] } },
+    { "id": "fighter-pick", "what": "Solo chosen, the setup with the fighter pick", "keys": ["ENTER"], "settleMs": 2500, "shot": "03-fighter-pick" },
+    { "id": "match-start", "what": "Start pressed; the match loads and begins", "keys": ["ENTER"], "settleMs": 20000, "shot": "04-match" },
+    { "id": "match-play", "what": "the match, after half a minute of play (the frame rate is read over this time)", "settleMs": 30000, "shot": "05-match-later" },
+    { "id": "pause", "what": "the pause menu", "keys": ["P"], "settleMs": 1800, "shot": "06-pause" },
+    { "id": "quit-question", "what": "Quit, and the question 'Close the game?' with Stay lit", "keys": ["DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "DOWN", "ENTER"], "settleMs": 1500, "shot": "07-quit-question" },
+    { "id": "close-the-game", "what": "Up to 'Close the game', Enter: the program must close", "keys": ["UP", "ENTER"], "settleMs": 500 }
